ionally  cheap but at the same time delivering as  good an outcome from a patient's  perspective in the 21st century data is  the energy or the fuel of transformation  anything you could measure you can  improve and data is one of the ways of  doing that 1 million people use the NHS  every 36 hours but there's no  centralized system where doctors can  access their medical data most patients  seeing me expects me to have all the  data from their general practice we need  to drive this integration between  primary care hospital and back into the  community you can actually predict  disease before you see the manifestation  of disease by segmenting the population  and identifying those at greater risk to  do this the NHS will have to tackle  fears over personal data being shared  sharing data is critical from a  patient's perspective and we need to win  the confidence of the public when it  comes to the privacy and security aspect  of data sharing  [Music]  the NHS is facing a funding gap by 2020  it's estimated to be 20 billion pounds  short a lot of people out there think  investing in health care is an a  bottomless pit  I could confidently tell you not just my  work look at the work The Lancet  Commission the world Innovation Summit  for health care the best return on  investment any country could make is in  health healthy nation means a productive  nation healthy nation means economic  growth for every pound you spend in  health you get two pounds back quality  should be the organizing principle of  any Health System it's a wonderful  future if we embrace it  [Music]

